Article 3 (Admission of Foreigners Subject to Removal, etc.)
(1) When an immigration control official working in a departure waiting room (hereinafter referred to as the "responsible official") admits a foreigner subject to removal to a departure waiting room, the official shall verify the passport and the written notice of denial of entry under Article 19 (2) of the Enforcement Rules of the Immigration Act, etc. The written notice of denial of entry may be verified through the immigration information system.
(2) Upon admission, a foreigner subject to removal shall complete and submit to the responsible official a questionnaire containing the following matters. Where the foreigner cannot complete it personally, the responsible official may prepare it on his or her behalf after confirming the answers:
1. Whether the foreigner wishes to change the place of waiting for removal under the proviso to Article 76-2 (1) of the Immigration Act;
2. The foreigner's health condition, including illness, physical disability, and injuries;
3. Whether the foreigner wishes to have valuables and other belongings stored.
(3) The head, etc. shall designate an official responsible for special protection, including humanitarian treatment, for any admitted foreigner who falls under any of the following:
1. A patient;
2. A pregnant woman;
3. An elderly or infirm person;
4. A person under 19 years of age;
5. A person awaiting removal for a prolonged period due to proceedings for relief of rights under the Immigration Act or other statutes;
6. Any other person comparable to subparagraphs 1 through 5 whom the head, etc. deems in need of special protection.
(4) An official designated under paragraph (3) shall endeavor to ensure appropriate treatment of the relevant admitted foreigner with respect to room assignment, meals, medical care, safety, etc.
